OL,3,GNEWSAPuffin at Tees Barrage 'an
OL,4,Aextremely rare sight'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA sighting of a puffin on the Tees
OL,7,FBarrage has been described by a
OL,8,Fbirdwatcher as extremely rare.
OL,10,FPuffins usually live out at sea or
OL,11,Fduring the breeding season on coastal
OL,12,Fcliffs or offshore islands. One was
OL,13,Fspotted at the structure, which stands
OL,14,F22 miles (35km) from the mouth of the
OL,15,FRiver Tees, on Wednesday.
OL,17,FThe puffin has been paddling short
OL,18,Fdistances up and down the river, and
OL,19,Fpeople have been asked not to approach
OL,20,Fit.
OL,23,APub: 14-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
